From d7394ee152a3ec343bbeffaca7e6f712dda7bde4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Orsavio P. Delmare" <orsavio@delmare.lu>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:05:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 41/50] ath11k: move the nss-member fix to a late patch, and
 re-enable the NSS runtime

Editing 199-003 in place to unguard the nss members broke a later patch in
the series (the one adding bss_peer inside the same ifdef), which then failed
to apply: 'Hunk #1 FAILED at 710 ... core.h.rej'. Revert that edit and do it
as 999-941 instead, generated with diff against the fully-patched tree so the
context is exact.

Also adds 999-940, which prints the skb geometry when a CE rx buffer fails to
map -- that failure turned out to be a cascade from missing calibration data
rather than an NSS bug, but the warning as shipped says nothing useful about
which pipe or what the skb looked like.

And drops -nss-tools from the ECW336: with the caldata and 02_network fixes
in place, an NSS-enabled build comes up with all three radios (R_PHYN=3), no
swiotlb or HTC failures, and Ethernet passing traffic at 0.4 ms, so the
earlier reason for excluding the runtime no longer holds.
